# Gamma level look — captain lock (2026-08-15)

Source: Lavish design-consultation board `.lavish/gamma-level-look-board.html` (captain picks queued
2026-08-15, all six questions answered). Inputs folded: `data/tv-gamma-level-ux-pulse/report.md`,
`data/tv-gamma-level-look-voice/report.md`, `data/gamma-method-grill/codex-design-voice-2026-08-14.txt`,
`data/gamma-method-grill/north-star-2026-08-14.md`.

## Locked look (captain picks, verbatim option ids)

1. **Label (Q1=C, Q1b=C2):** `<strike> · GEX <nn>%` — e.g. `780 · GEX 22%`. Whole percents. Magnitude
   stub before the label text, scaled on a FIXED 0–30% GEX-share axis (never night-relative). Bare percent
   forbidden. Strike always printed on the line.
2. **Strength (Q2=S1):** rank-weighted lines — rank 1 solid 2px/90% opacity, rank 2 solid 1px/68%,
   rank 3 dotted 1px/48%. Labels never fade below 80% opacity. No shaded zones, no reach bars.
3. **Regime (Q3=R1+hover, Q3b=R1b):** one quiet `size.tiny` chip `GEX <MMM DD> CLOSE · <REGIME>`
   (e.g. `GEX AUG 13 CLOSE · STABILIZING`). Stale: regime word REPLACED by STALE
   (`GEX AUG 11 CLOSE · STALE`) and every level desaturates to grey — a stale regime claim is never shown.
   Every ranked-level hover carries a per-wall regime sentence:
   - Stabilizing: "dealer hedging tends to fade moves into this level today."
   - Amplifying: "dealer hedging can accelerate moves through this level today."
4. **Hover template (locked draft):**
   `Call Wall · rank 1 · 780.00` / `GEX 22.4% of side |net GEX| in ranked band · 1.8× next call strike` /
   regime sentence / `As of <date> close. Reference level, not a forecast.`
5. **Data freshness (Q4=I2):** nightly mint PLUS one morning refresh ~09:45 ET after opening flow, with
   the visible reload cue when a newer book exists (same pattern as tradingview-tools PR #95). Chip shows
   the mint time for the morning book. Levels never move silently mid-session (platform mints once per load).
6. **Flip:** dotted, own hue, labeled `flip` — visually unlike any wall (unchanged from proposal).
7. **Never:** shaded zones, rank-only tokens as level names, bare percent, silent restyles.
   Palette: calls cyan family, puts ember family; red/green stays owned by candles.

## Explicitly not chosen

- Glyph-only label (B), stub-only label (D), `GEX SHARE` full wording (C1), percent-first (C3),
  mixed verbosity (C4), two-line label (C5).
- Reach-bars strength grammar (S2) — offered including a later-trial option; captain took plain S1.
- Regime-as-wall-texture (R2). Corner dashboard chips beyond the single R1b chip.
- Hourly refresh (I3); nightly-only (I1); defer-to-calibration (I4).

## Consequences

- Chart flips from two walls to all ranked levels (top-3/side, 3% floor, gex-v1.2 #97 rule) once this
  look ships; review trims, never reveals.
- Ship task: implement the look in the gamma levels template (no-mistakes, Pine brain dispatch).
- Infra task: morning-refresh pipeline run + publish + reload-cue wiring (separate work item).
